<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lelantine War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 8th–7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lelantine War was a conflict between the Euboean cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> and Eretria over the fertile Lelantine plain that lay between them, fought around the late 8th or early 7th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a> said it drew allies from much of the Greek world, making it the first war beyond local quarrels. Its course is obscure, but Eretria seems to have come off worse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lelantine-war.jpg" alt="Lelantine War" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: T8612 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lelantine_War.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
